course: dictionary
lesson: 8639
title: Seabed: the ground under the sea
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Seabed is made of two small words, sea and bed. Put them together and you get the bed of the sea, which is the ground at the bottom of the water. «An anchor is a heavy hook that digs into the seabed to hold the ship.» The anchor has to reach the bottom of the sea, so seabed must mean the sea floor.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «A flounder lies flat on the seabed, flicks sand over its edges and changes its pattern to match.» A flat fish that hides under sand needs ground to lie on, so the seabed is the sand and mud at the bottom of the sea. Try your meaning in the sentence: "A flounder lies flat on the ground at the bottom of the sea" still makes sense.
explain: Seabed is a noun, so it names a thing. You can write the seabed, or seabeds when you mean more than one part of the sea floor. Phrases such as on the seabed, deep seabed and sink to the seabed show you how it is used. The ocean floor means nearly the same thing.
fact: The seabed is the ground at the bottom of the sea.
fact: Seabed is made from the words sea and bed, and it means the same as the ocean floor.
fact: The seabed can be sand, mud, rocks, coral or even mountains.
fact: «Grey whales feed by sucking mud from the seabed.»
fact: Shells and shipwrecks lie on the seabed, and divers and robot submarines explore it.
exercise: «A flounder lies flat on the seabed.» What is the seabed? | The top of the waves | *The ground at the bottom of the sea | A tall rock above the sea | A boat's deck
exercise: Which of these things can be found on the seabed? | *Shipwrecks and shells | Birds that fly high | Clouds and rain | Trees and grass
exercise: «Grey whales feed by sucking mud from the seabed.» Where do grey whales get their food? | *From the mud at the bottom of the sea | From the surface of the waves | In the air above the clouds | From a farm on land
test: Seabed is made from which two words? | Sea and bread | Sun and bread | *Sea and bed | Sand and bed
test: Which of these is another name for the seabed? | Shoreline | *Ocean floor | Waves | Sky
exam: Which sentence uses seabed correctly? | We drank the seabed on a hot day. | The seabed is a kind of bird that sings. | *Divers swim down to explore the seabed. | The seabed rose up into the blue sky.
